---
/**
 * The /scorecard headline (docs/projects/redesign/design-export-remaining/design_handoff_scorecard,
 * band 1).
 *
 * The site's hero with no right-hand block: H1 then a statement, with the fill left on its default
 * `--agents`, because the scorecard is an agents surface. No fill variant class is added for that
 * reason.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE IS `.rd-hero` IN global.css, shared with the other eight heroes — including the
 * clamp ceiling and the 32ch lede. The lede is a direct child rather than a row item here, so this
 * file keeps the two things a row would otherwise give it: the space under the H1 and the entry
 * rise. Both are written on two classes so they outrank the shared rule.
 *
 * THE H1 CLAMP CEILING IS THE SITEWIDE 176px, same as every sibling hero. It was 118px, on the
 * bundle's claim that "Scorecard" wraps at 176. Measured on the rendered page across 320px to
 * 3840px on 2026-08-23, it does not: the word is one line at every width, and the cap only starts
 * binding at a 1467px viewport, where 176px renders "Scorecard" 737px wide inside a 1100px column
 * — 363px to spare. It cannot wrap in any case, because `.rd-fill` is `white-space: nowrap`.
 *
 * Below 720px the shared collapse pins 68px, so the ceiling never applies there and raising it
 * changed nothing at mobile widths.
 *
 * IT CARRIES `data-module='scorecard-hero'` AND NO `.modern-skin`, since 2026-08-29: this is the
 * only /scorecard hero in the document and retro restyles it in place, under that module prefix in
 * src/styles/retro.css. The prefix is load-bearing — Astro appends a `[data-astro-cid-…]` to the
 * selectors below and that attribute counts as a class, so a retro rule without it loses silently.
 */
---

{/*
  A div, not a section — the same call WritingHero.astro, ProjectsHero.astro and AboutHero.astro
  made: `npm run validate:html` names an h1 inside sectioning content, and an unnamed <section> is
  not exposed as a region anyway.
*/}
<div class="rd-section rd-hero scorecard-hero" data-module="scorecard-hero">
  <h1><span class="rd-fill">Scorecard</span></h1>
  <p class="hero-statement">This site's own scores, measured nightly.</p>
</div>

<style>
  .scorecard-hero { padding-top: 72px; }

  .scorecard-hero .hero-statement {
    margin-top: 32px;
    animation: riseIn .7s ease .12s both;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .scorecard-hero { padding-top: 52px; }

    .scorecard-hero .hero-statement { margin-top: 24px; }
  }
</style>
